From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 18:45:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/31] qwen4exp seqpar prototype: token-split hyper-connection
 work in 2-GPU -sm tensor prefill (LLAMA_SEQPAR=1, default off)

New op GGML_OP_TOKEN_SCATTER (ggml_token_scatter): on a single backend a copy; on the meta backend its
output is split along the token axis in equal halves. Right behind a partial sum's reduce point the meta
backend replaces that all-reduce by a reduce-scatter (new comm hook; CUDA copy-engine implementation with
the same bf16 rounding as the CE all-reduce); otherwise each device copies its slice of a mirrored input.
ALL_GATHER accepts a split along the slowest axis (new comm all-gather hook through the CE scratch, chunked).
DSV4_HC_PRE/POST accept operands consistently split along their token axis.

qwen4exp: with LLAMA_SEQPAR=1, 2 meta devices, -sm tensor and an even ubatch >= LLAMA_SEQPAR_MIN (512) the
residual streams stay token-split from layer 0 to the last layer; each block gathers its hc_mixed input,
the shared expert runs on local tokens, the attention and MoE outputs are reduce-scattered
(LLAMA_SEQPAR_RS bitmask, default 3). PLE layers and the last layer run on gathered streams.
Off: graph unchanged.
